      "problem": "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the lateral surface area $S$ of the right cone if the base radius is $r=6,$ and the slant height is $l=10.$",
      "worked_solution": "The  lateral surface area of the right cone is $S=\\pi rl.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(rl) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂l})\\,\\text{d}l \\\\  & =\\pi l\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi r\\,\\text{d}l\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6,$ and $l=10,$  the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(6,10) & =10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
